# Cataclysm 0.9 implementation

Selected candidates: **designer** (Runic Relic subsystem) and **researcher** (Companion Squad Special Abilities). Both integrated in `docs/preview/game.js`, `index.html`, and `game.css`. No frozen baseline, configuration, dependencies, metadata, tests, or publishing code changed.

## Implementation and contracts

- Designer: retained existing shield immunity and 260-unit enemy slow aura, six-second duration and ten-second activation cooldown. Extracted `spawnRelic()`, with first arrival at 35 seconds (preserved baseline), subsequent arrivals 45 seconds after a successful spawn, maximum three ground items, map-clamped positions 160 units from the player. `updateRelics(dt)` handles automatic pickup, expiration and readiness; `activateRunicRelic()` gates activation by actual running state and cooldown. Added spawn, pickup, expiry and readiness cues. The existing `runic-relic-activate` button now includes an accessible state label and displays cooldown even after the effect ends.
- Researcher: `summonCompanion()` initializes per-role readiness, cooldown and duration. Recruitment remains through existing upgrade offers; training retains cooldown rather than resetting it. `companionSpecialAbilityActivate(type)` implements a 16-projectile radial burst (18s cooldown), healing pulse (24s), and tank guard/nearby taunt (6s effect, 18s cooldown). Guard adds capped damage mitigation and attracts nearby enemies, while collision damage still measures distance to the player. Burst respects the 160-projectile budget and squad damage/count/bounce investments. Healing restores the player, because companions have no individual HP pools; allies flash together. This is the explicit adaptation of “group healing” to the existing runtime.
- `updateCompanions(dt)` advances cooldowns and guard duration in simulation seconds, with readiness notices and sounds. Timers freeze during pause/upgrade selection. Restart constructs clean relic and companion state. Existing score, upgrades, persisted best/completed runs, auto-fire, tactics, keyboard, pointer release/cancellation and read-only diagnostic interfaces remain intact. New companion timers are included automatically in existing copied companion snapshots.
- UI: `companionAbilityButtons` holds three initially hidden buttons, one per recruited role, with disabled cooldown states, countdown text, progress backgrounds and ARIA labels. A separate responsive bottom row keeps these clear of core action buttons; touch targets are at least 44px. Relic and companion activations do not clear movement input; repeated clicks are rejected by simulation state. Tank guard receives an outline; existing reduced-motion rendering and mute policies apply.
- Contract adaptation: `spawnRelic` is exported as `window.spawnRelic` from the existing classic script. An ES-module `export` would break the preserved loading model. Other named functions are internal, connected to real buttons and the existing tick loop. No writable test API was shipped.
- Release identity and boot consistency check updated to 0.9; `game-version` is preserved for runner stamping.

## Evidence and deferred ledger

Read job.json, plan.json (including update selection), feedback.md (`[]`), the roadmap and existing runtime. The private evidence analyst/Council stage is upstream; this Coder did not access raw footage, speech or private transcript. No independent source timestamps were supplied. Council feature proposals remain design hypotheses, not verified player requests.

| Item / source | State / dependency / uncertainty |
| --- | --- |
| Relics / designer selection | Implemented; existing pickups and buff hooks completed, bounded objects and simulation timers |
| Role abilities / researcher selection | Implemented; depends on recruitment, squad stats, projectile budget and shared HP model |
| UI crowding / Critic | Responsive separate row implemented; browser/physical-device geometry remains unverified |
| Enemy mutation / rejected engineer proposal | Deferred by Producer; requires readable telegraphs, encounter pacing and combined-buff balance tests |
| Power-gated tiers / roadmap hypothesis | Deferred; requires measured sustained effectiveness, smoothing and hysteresis before changing current time unlocks |
| Population-aware director / roadmap hypothesis | Deferred; existing population cap and spawn floor preserved; needs threat budgets and recovery pacing |
| New late-run encounters/environment / roadmap | Deferred; depends on director and unlock contracts, not authorized this release |
| Obstacles / viewer proposal | Deferred; requires collision/pathfinding and performance work |
| Emergency attack / viewer proposal | Burst now offers recruited-shooter radial attack; universal emergency attack remains unselected |
| Enemy diversity, music / viewer proposals | Existing threat variants and music/mute retained; no duplicate implementation |
| Local HP bar / viewer proposal | Deferred; existing HP HUD preserved, local player bar remains unselected |
| Full evidence ledger / roadmap | Upstream evidence requirement; no private transcript supplied here, so no invented exhaustive recording ledger |

## Verification

- `node --check docs/preview/game.js`: passed.
- `node game_factory/mobile_acceptance.cjs`: attempted once; blocked before loading any game page. Chrome crashed at launch: `setsockopt: Operation not permitted`, SIGTRAP. No browser gameplay pass, independent QA approval, deployment or physical-phone verification is claimed.
- Node VM integration harness below executes the actual source with an in-memory test-only internal export and mock DOM/canvas. The first draft failed due to a missing mock `innerWidth`; a second draft needed a mock gradient object for rendering. The combined-load extension also required upgrade-card DOM mocks. These were harness issues, not runtime game failures. Final results are recorded below after execution. The fixture grants HP and continues upgrade dialogs to inspect 21-minute progression, not to represent unaided player survival. CPU timing excludes real browser rendering and is not a mobile-performance measurement.

