Final harness outcome: **PASS**. Simulated 1,260 seconds at 30 updates/second with all three companions recruited and repeated ability activation attempts every two seconds. Maximum observed population: **95 enemies**; maximum observed projectiles: **19** (asserted budget ≤160); ground relic budget asserted ≤3 throughout. Gas tier available at 1,200s; initial tier restricted to shambler; difficulty increased over the run. Combined-load simulation took **6,661 ms** in this environment with mock drawing. Separate lifecycle assertions cover pickup, six-second expiry, ten-second cooldown, hidden/unlocked controls, damage mitigation, healing, burst count, repeated-click rejection and pause/restart. `git diff --check` also passed.

Remaining limitations: no browser geometry, touch hit-testing, real rendering performance, audio playback, physical-device or independent QA result could be established here because Chrome could not launch. The 21-minute invulnerable fixture is a bounded-state regression check, not a balance assessment or measured survival target. Enemy slow and shield combat behavior are preserved existing hooks inspected in source; the harness checks relic activation/expiry rather than validating every enemy behavior against both effects. Private recording ingestion remains the upstream analyst's responsibility. Human usability and balance of simultaneous relic/role actions remain open for the following roadmap cycle.
